! The Salt-Stair

''Stratum:'' the sea-level ring — ''host town unnamed (prompt)'' · ''Scale:'' Site (one room).

A small market lararium ''three alleys down from the harbor steps'' — one room wide, smelling
of roasted beans and low tide. The dish over the lintel steams for ordinary guests and flares
blue-white for extraordinary ones. A deep booth further in from the door carries a privacy ward
older than the shop — the booth ward "predates the log, predates the shop, possibly predates
warding." A faerie corner booth runs long campaign nights with their own Lares, streaming to
Cabal-realm nakama. A shelf takes hole-drilled coins; the house keeps them where the light
lands first.

''Scene canon:'' the Patroness took the deep booth here on the eve of the company's sailing
(`lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/campaign/salt-stair-booth`, referee-side).

''Open at the counter:'' MUG-SMOKE keeps the Spice Quarter compitale, and something wearing the
same manner pours here. One spirit working two rooms, a lineage sharing a name, or two spirits
who have never met — the Salt-Stair declines to say, and MUG-SMOKE has never been asked directly.

